# LPC2148 – Switch Controlled LED

## Aim
To write an Embedded C Program for the LPC214x microcontroller to read the status of switch pin P0.4 and control LED pin P0.8 accordingly.

## Hardware Requirements
- LPC2148 Microcontroller
- Push Button Switch
- LED
- Connecting Wires

## Pin Connections

| Component | LPC2148 Pin |
|---|---|
| Switch | P0.4 |
| LED | P0.8 |

## Working Principle
- P0.4 is configured as an input pin.
- P0.8 is configured as an output pin.
- The program continuously monitors the switch status using the IOPIN0 register.
- When P0.4 is HIGH, IOSET0 is used to turn ON the LED.
- When P0.4 is LOW, IOCLR0 is used to turn OFF the LED.

## Registers Used

| Register | Function |
|---|---|
| IODIR0 | Configures GPIO pins as input or output |
| IOPIN0 | Reads the current pin status |
| IOSET0 | Sets the output pin HIGH |
| IOCLR0 | Clears the output pin LOW |

## Program Logic
1. Configure P0.4 as input.
2. Configure P0.8 as output.
3. Read the switch status continuously.
4. If the switch is HIGH, turn ON the LED.
5. If the switch is LOW, turn OFF the LED.

## Expected Output

| Switch P0.4 | LED P0.8 |
|---|---|
| HIGH (1) | ON |
| LOW (0) | OFF
